error BYN2305: argument for `width` must be named

  5 │ print($"{area(3, height: 4)}");
    │               ^
    │
  help: name them so they cannot be swapped; `area` has several `i64` parameters
    │ 5 │ print($"{area(width: 3, height: 4)}");
    │   │               +++++++

error BYN2305: argument for `verbose` must be named

  6 │ show(true);
    │      ^^^^
    │
  help: write `verbose: …`; a `bool` argument says nothing at the call site
    │ 6 │ show(verbose: true);
    │   │      +++++++++
